/* DISCOVERY / derivation (CONTRIBUTION 3, publishable upgrade): the FORMAL van Trees (Bayesian
   Cramer-Rao) inequality that result 20 ASSUMED. Van Trees: for a Bayesian model (prior pi on theta,
   observations X ~ p(x|theta)) and ANY estimator theta_hat, the Bayes risk obeys
       E[(theta_hat - theta)^2] >= 1 / (I_data + I_prior),
   where I_prior = prior Fisher information, I_data = E_theta[Fisher info of the likelihood]. Unlike
   ordinary Cramer-Rao, this applies to SEQUENTIAL/adaptive designs and to ANY (even biased) estimator.
   Proof: Cauchy-Schwarz on the Bayesian score psi = d/dtheta log(pi(theta) p(X|theta)) --
   1 = (E[psi*Delta])^2 <= E[psi^2] E[Delta^2] = (I_data+I_prior) * MSE, Delta = theta_hat - theta. This
   is the floor C/m_t of result 20, now proved (the m_t is exactly I_prior + accumulated I_data). Maxima
   is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

/* Gaussian-Gaussian conjugate instance where van Trees is TIGHT: prior theta ~ N(mu0, tau^2), n obs
   x_i = theta + N(0,sigma^2). Prior info J = 1/tau^2, per-obs info I = 1/sigma^2. */
J : 1/tau^2$
Ipe : 1/sigma^2$
total : J + n*Ipe$
vtbound : 1/total$
print("prior info J = 1/tau^2 ; per-obs info I = 1/sigma^2 ; total info after n obs =", total)$
print("van Trees bound 1/(I_data + I_prior) =", ratsimp(vtbound))$

/* the Gaussian-Gaussian posterior variance (the Bayes-optimal MSE) equals the van Trees bound: TIGHT */
postvar : 1/(1/tau^2 + n/sigma^2)$
print("Gaussian posterior variance (Bayes MSE) =", ratsimp(postvar))$
print("tightness check: vtbound - postvar =", ratsimp(vtbound - postvar), " (0 => van Trees is TIGHT)")$

/* the Cauchy-Schwarz core (proved in Rocq): with the score identity E[psi*Delta] = 1 and the info
   decomposition E[psi^2] = total, MSE >= 1^2 / total = 1/(I_data + I_prior). */
print("Cauchy-Schwarz: (E[psi*Delta])^2 <= E[psi^2] * E[Delta^2] ; E[psi*Delta]=1, E[psi^2]=total")$
print("=> 1 <= total * MSE => MSE >= 1/total  (Rocq: cauchy_schwarz + van_trees_inequality)")$

/* CONFOUNDING reduces the per-obs IDENTIFYING information (fraction Vid<1 of the variation identifies
   the causal effect), so I_data drops to n*Vid/sigma^2 and the floor 1/(J + n*Vid/sigma^2) is HIGHER
   -- the Bayesian/sequential analogue of results 10 and 12. */
Iconf : Vid/sigma^2$
print("confounded per-obs info = Vid/sigma^2 (Vid<1) => floor 1/(J + n*Vid/sigma^2) HIGHER")$
print("floor ratio confounded/experimental =",
      ratsimp((1/(J + n*Iconf))/(1/(J + n*Ipe))), " >= 1 for Vid <= 1")$
